# Optional: use your own TURN relay instead of the free public one.
#
# You do not need any of this. Out of the box the app falls back to Metered's
# Open Relay, which is free, needs no account, and allows 20GB of relayed
# traffic a month shared across everyone using it.
#
# Set your own only if you would rather not share that quota - a free account at
# metered.ca gives you credentials, and Cloudflare and Twilio both offer relays
# too. ALL THREE values are required; a partial set is ignored on purpose,
# because a relay with the wrong credentials does not fail loudly, it just
# quietly never connects.
#
# These are compiled into the JavaScript that ships to the browser, so treat
# them as public. That is unavoidable for a browser app with no backend to mint
# short-lived credentials, and it is why the default is a relay whose
# credentials are published anyway. Never put anything genuinely secret here.
#
# On Vercel: Project Settings -> Environment Variables, then redeploy.

# VITE_TURN_URLS=turn:your.relay:3478,turns:your.relay:5349
# VITE_TURN_USERNAME=your-username
# VITE_TURN_CREDENTIAL=your-credential
